            <ArticleTitle>Catamenial Bernard-Horner's syndrome related to thoracic endometriosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e24-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the case of a young woman with a recurrent right Bernard-Horner's syndrome associated with the onset of intermittent supraclavicular mass. Surgical excision of the mass revealed the endometrial pattern of the tumor and the close relationship between Bernard-Horner's syndrome and thoracic endometriosis. No other case of this syndrome has been reported in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
